{# Transcribed from the static design mockup (thank-you page)'s <main> grid. Extends
   layouts/checkout.twig — same header-checkout/footer-compliance partials as
   checkout.twig. layouts/checkout.twig's <main> class is now an overridable
   `main_class` block; this page overrides it below with the mockup's own
   `lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-x-10` (the layout's bare-default `lg:grid
   lg:grid-cols-2`, used by checkout.twig, was missing this page's `lg:gap-x-10`).

   Every order, contact, shipping, payment and totals figure now comes from the
   `receipt` view model the controller renders with — the durable snapshot of the
   local order rows, so a refresh shows the same page as the first load.

   `receipt.hasOrder()` is the one structural branch. A journey whose orders could
   not be read still reaches this page by design — an accounting failure must not
   lock a buyer out of their own receipt — so the summary column and the order
   details card are omitted rather than drawn empty, and what is left says the one
   thing that is still true: the intake was received and is pending review.

   No page JS: this page has no inline scripts of its own in the mockup (only
   lucide.createIcons() + the shared script.js, both already handled by the
   base/layout templates). #}
{% extends 'layouts/checkout.twig' %}
{% set page_title = 'Order Confirmed' %}
{% set page_description = 'Your AsterMD order is confirmed and pending physician review.' %}
{% block main_class %}lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-x-10{% endblock %}
{% block content %}

  <!-- ==================== CONFIRMATION ==================== -->
  <div class="px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 lg:py-14 lg:pl-24 lg:pr-0">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[500px] flex flex-col gap-6 lg:mx-0 lg:ml-auto">

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-primary">
          <i data-lucide="check" class="size-5 text-primary" stroke-width="3"></i>
        </span>
        <div>
          {# The first placed reference is the order the buyer will quote to support.
             Omitted rather than shown as "Order #" when there is none to name. #}
          {% if receipt.orderNumber %}
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Order #{{ receipt.orderNumber }}</p>
          {% endif %}
          {# Greeted by nothing rather than by a placeholder when the stored name is
             empty: "Thank you, !" is worse than "Thank you!". #}
          <h1 class="font-heading text-[24px] font-bold text-heading sm:text-[28px]">{% if receipt.buyerFirstName %}Thank you, <span id="thankyou-name">{{ receipt.buyerFirstName }}</span>!{% else %}Thank you!{% endif %}</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== DELIVERY MAP ==================== -->
      {# Also gated on there being an address: a map centred on nowhere is worse
         than no map. #}
      {% if maps_api_key and receipt.shippingAddress %}
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?key={{ maps_api_key }}&q={{ receipt.shippingAddress|url_encode }}"
          class="h-[220px] w-full border-0"
          loading="lazy"
          referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
          title="Shipping address map"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- ==================== STATUS CARD ==================== -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-6">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading">Intake Received &amp; Pending Review</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          We've received your submission and placed your order on hold. Our licensed physician is currently reviewing your health information to see if this treatment is right for you.
        </p>
        {# No patient-portal URL is configured, so this link is a placeholder. #}
        <a href="#" class="mt-6 inline-flex h-[41px] w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm bg-primary px-5 text-base font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary-hover focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary-hover">
          Go to Patient Portal
          <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="size-[14px]"></i>
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== WHAT HAPPENS NEXT ==================== -->
      {# The mockup's `Case ID: PMD1493450` is gone from this header. The clinical
         record carries no case id at the moment a treatment is created, so an
         unconditional render prints a fiction and a conditional one prints an
         empty label on every real order. Reading a real one back is later work. #}
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-6">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading">What happens next?</h2>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-5">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <p class="text-base font-medium text-heading">Provider / Doctor Review</p>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-warning-light px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-warning">
                <i data-lucide="hourglass" class="size-3"></i>
                In Progress
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-3 flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-warning-light">
                <i data-lucide="user-search" class="size-4 text-warning"></i>
              </span>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Our clinical team is currently reviewing your intake forms and health information. This typically takes 24-48 hours.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <p class="text-base font-medium text-heading">Prescription &amp; Delivery</p>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-surface px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-muted">
                <i data-lucide="circle-pause" class="size-3"></i>
                On Hold
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-3 flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-surface">
                <i data-lucide="truck" class="size-4 text-icon-muted"></i>
              </span>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">If approved, your prescription will be sent to our pharmacy and shipped discreetly to your address. If additional information is needed, your doctor will message you.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== ORDER DETAILS ==================== -->
      {% if receipt.hasOrder() %}
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-6">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading">Order details</h2>

        {# Territory and postal code share a line in the mockup, so they are joined
           once here and used by both address blocks below. #}
        {% set region = (receipt.shipping.territory ~ ' ' ~ receipt.shipping.postal_code)|trim %}

        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {# Each block below is omitted rather than drawn as a bare heading when
             the receipt has nothing to put under it. #}
          {% if receipt.buyerEmail or receipt.buyerPhone %}
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">Contact information</p>
            {% if receipt.buyerEmail %}
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-body">{{ receipt.buyerEmail }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if receipt.buyerPhone %}
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-body">{{ receipt.buyerPhone }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {# The mockup badges the card as Mastercard. The order row keeps four
             digits and nothing else — no scheme is recorded anywhere — so the
             badge is dropped rather than guessed at, and the whole block is
             omitted when even the four digits are missing. #}
          {% if receipt.cardLastFour %}
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">Payment method</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-body">Card ending in {{ receipt.cardLastFour }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endif %}

          {% if receipt.shipping.name or receipt.shippingAddress %}
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">Shipping address</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
              {% if receipt.shipping.name %}{{ receipt.shipping.name }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.address_line %}{{ receipt.shipping.address_line }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.city %}{{ receipt.shipping.city }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if region %}{{ region }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.country %}{{ receipt.shipping.country }}{% endif %}
            </p>
          </div>
          {# The mockup shows a second, different billing address. There is no
             separate billing address in this deployment — the card is billed to the
             shipping address — so the same block is repeated rather than a second
             set of fields invented. A reader who expects two addresses is reading
             the mockup, not the data. #}
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">Billing address</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
              {% if receipt.shipping.name %}{{ receipt.shipping.name }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.address_line %}{{ receipt.shipping.address_line }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.city %}{{ receipt.shipping.city }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if region %}{{ region }}<br />{% endif %}
              {% if receipt.shipping.country %}{{ receipt.shipping.country }}{% endif %}
            </p>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# The mockup's `DHL Ecommerce Parcel Direct - 5 to 9 business days` block is
           gone: nobody chose a courier. There are no shipping lines in this
           deployment and `app.features.shipping_selector` is off, so naming a
           carrier here would be naming one at random. #}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ==================== ORDER SUMMARY ==================== -->
  {# Omitted entirely with no order to summarise, rather than drawn as an empty
     panel with zeroes in it. #}
  {% if receipt.hasOrder() %}
  <div class="border-border bg-background-2 px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 lg:border-l lg:px-12 lg:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[410px] lg:mx-0 lg:sticky lg:top-10">

      <!-- ==================== LINE ITEMS ==================== -->
      {# The receipt's stored lines are the durable order snapshot — slug, name,
         kind, quantity and price — so there is no product image and no plan name
         to render: neither is part of what was charged, and re-reading the catalog
         here would let a later price or a renamed variant rewrite a kept receipt.
         Every line therefore gets the mockup's placeholder tile, with the same
         `pill` icon checkout.twig already uses for a line with no image. #}
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        {% for line in receipt.lines %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="relative shrink-0">
            <span class="flex size-14 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-surface">
              <i data-lucide="pill" class="size-6 text-icon-muted"></i>
            </span>
            <span class="absolute -right-1.5 -top-1.5 flex size-5 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-heading text-xs font-medium text-background">{{ line.quantity }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <p class="text-sm text-heading">{{ line.name }}</p>
          </div>
          {# A free attachment shows at 0¢ rather than being hidden, exactly as it
             did on the checkout summary: a supply the buyer is receiving belongs on
             the receipt whether or not it was charged for. #}
          <p class="shrink-0 text-base font-medium text-heading">{{ line.line_total_cents|money }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {# The mockup's disabled discount-code box is gone. Nothing can be applied to
         an order that has already been charged, and an input that can never be
         enabled invites a buyer to try. #}

      <!-- ==================== TOTALS ==================== -->
      {# No shipping and no tax rows, for the same reason the checkout summary has
         none: the total is exactly subtotal minus discount, in integer cents.
         `Consultation Fee — Included` stays because it is true of the price, not a
         line item that was added to it. #}
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-border pt-6 text-sm text-heading">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Subtotal • {{ receipt.itemCount }} item{{ receipt.itemCount == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>
          <span>{{ receipt.subtotalCents|money }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Consultation Fee</span>
          <span>Included</span>
        </div>
        {% if receipt.hasDiscount() %}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span>Discount{% if receipt.promotionCode %} • {{ receipt.promotionCode }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span>−{{ receipt.discountCents|money }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-border pt-4">
        <span class="text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading">Total</span>
        <span class="text-base font-medium sm:text-lg text-heading"><span class="mr-1 text-sm font-normal text-muted align-middle">{{ receipt.currency }}</span>{{ receipt.paidTotalCents|money }}</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ==================== PAYMENT NOTICE ==================== -->
      {# The mockup said the card was only authorized and would not be charged
         unless a doctor approved the prescription. That is not what happens here:
         the charge is single-step and the money has already moved by the time this
         page renders, so the notice says so. Skipped when nothing was charged. #}
      {% if receipt.paidTotalCents > 0 %}
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-sm border border-primary bg-primary-light px-4 py-4">
        <i data-lucide="info" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary"></i>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-heading">Your card has been charged {{ receipt.paidTotalCents|money }}. Your order is on hold until a licensed physician has reviewed your information.</p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

{% endblock %}
